WEBVTT

00:12.240 --> 00:14.990
Why is it Sasame?

00:14.990 --> 00:19.910
That was just a mistake, right, Akashi?

00:22.790 --> 00:26.750
I didn't do anything to make you hate me, right?

00:27.380 --> 00:30.210
So

00:31.050 --> 00:32.550
Akashi...

00:45.730 --> 00:54.070
The ink on today's graffiti runs

00:54.070 --> 01:05.080
A bicycle that has been abandoned awaits someone's return

01:05.080 --> 01:16.050
When we realized, it was up for us to choose if our existence is a replica or not

01:16.050 --> 01:20.430
Where is our proof?

01:20.430 --> 01:25.520
It's mankinds nature to come together

01:25.520 --> 01:30.570
Our love and bonds are things we can trust

01:30.570 --> 01:35.360
My sins are to be doubted

01:35.360 --> 01:41.700
The light I saw when you first held out your right hand

01:45.080 --> 01:50.540
We really are

01:59.050 --> 02:01.260
The Dark Metal

02:05.980 --> 02:10.480
Episode 20
Overlapping Sound of Love

02:14.820 --> 02:16.570
We went to Yomijima.

02:17.530 --> 02:19.200
The ocean was very beautiful.

02:20.160 --> 02:23.410
When you saw the ocean, you told me that

02:23.410 --> 02:26.080
you recalled nostalgic and happy things, Sasame.

02:27.250 --> 02:29.580
You'll have to tell me about those things sometime.

02:42.970 --> 02:46.270
It's not like you don't already
know about the Yomijima tragedy.

02:46.680 --> 02:49.350
What are you talking about?

02:49.350 --> 02:51.600
So you're going to continue to play dumb?

02:51.600 --> 02:54.520
Before that, if the repairs are done on the MA-Vesses,

02:54.520 --> 02:58.070
you are to resume the Lightless Realm survey at once.

02:58.070 --> 02:59.200
I cannot do that.

02:59.200 --> 03:03.200
Going in recklessly with the Corpse fully
recovered will be repeating things all over again.

03:04.410 --> 03:05.660
It's an order!

03:05.660 --> 03:10.620
Excuse me for saying this, but I doubt you can properly assess the situation.

03:11.040 --> 03:15.340
Therefore, I'd like you to grant me full authority.

03:15.340 --> 03:16.500
Suzaki!

03:16.500 --> 03:17.590
That's too arbitrary!

03:17.590 --> 03:22.800
If you say you cannot, then do this yourselves.

03:22.800 --> 03:28.430
That is, if you're willing to shoulder all responsibility without Senoh or Natsuiri here any longer.

03:32.900 --> 03:34.020
We're all in agreement, then?

03:34.860 --> 03:40.570
None of those guys understand a thing—
not even the sins they committed.

03:40.860 --> 03:45.160
Team Gargouille's main goal will be to suppress the Corpse.

03:45.620 --> 03:50.620
But that won't hold the meaning of erasing IX's past.

03:50.960 --> 03:54.330
Will defeating the Corpse really solve everything?

03:54.330 --> 03:56.670
Kasane, if you please.

03:57.460 --> 03:58.590
Sure.

03:59.130 --> 04:05.600
The Lightless Realm's source is almost
certainly the Lightless Stone in the Corpse.

04:05.600 --> 04:08.100
I'd like to study it in detail.

04:08.100 --> 04:11.430
I'm sure it holds all the answers.

04:11.850 --> 04:16.110
Which means nothing will begin until we defeat the Corpse.

04:16.860 --> 04:22.490
Didn't Natsuiri once say we could cure people of Necrometal by studying it?

04:22.820 --> 04:23.990
He did say that.

04:25.870 --> 04:28.830
Maybe Emiru and Sasame could be...

04:39.380 --> 04:42.800
A lot of the lab workers are gone now.

04:43.720 --> 04:47.600
I'm sure they all had other futures they wanted to pursue.

04:48.600 --> 04:53.390
Yet Tsugumi-san and everyone else on Yomijima...

04:54.190 --> 04:55.230
Mahmu...

04:56.270 --> 05:03.190
I'm not sure if someone like me can save everyone.

05:04.400 --> 05:08.410
We may be able to do something, but just as well as may not be.

05:09.280 --> 05:12.080
We're unsure of what we're able to do.

05:12.660 --> 05:13.540
Right...

05:14.080 --> 05:16.960
In the end, it's all self-satisfaction.

05:18.670 --> 05:21.500
But I think that's fine now too.

05:21.500 --> 05:24.840
It means we're doing our best
so that we don't regret anything.

05:26.220 --> 05:32.010
I want Sasame and Emiru back, and I'll do my best for that.

05:32.560 --> 05:34.980
Isn't that enough?

05:37.650 --> 05:40.570
I guess these will be our meals for a while.

05:45.360 --> 05:46.280
Akashi?

05:46.820 --> 05:47.530
Kasane-san.

05:47.530 --> 05:48.570
Akashi...

05:48.570 --> 05:50.410
Can we talk a bit?

05:50.410 --> 05:52.030
Great timing.

05:52.030 --> 05:54.290
I wanted to talk to you too.

05:54.290 --> 05:55.580
What is it?

05:55.580 --> 05:58.790
Something about your resonance with the Argent the other day...

06:00.630 --> 06:02.380
Guess I'll go eat with Raika.

06:05.800 --> 06:07.380
Are you all right?

06:07.380 --> 06:09.220
You've been pale since this morning.

06:10.300 --> 06:11.850
I'm fine.

06:11.850 --> 06:14.270
More importantly, what happened back then?

06:15.640 --> 06:16.600
What do you mean?

06:17.270 --> 06:21.480
You showed unimaginable levels of resonance with the Argent.

06:23.520 --> 06:25.740
Did it feel different than usual?

06:25.740 --> 06:28.820
Well, it's true that it felt strange.

06:28.820 --> 06:31.950
It was as if the Argent was lighter than my body.

06:31.950 --> 06:33.120
What about the LIM?

06:33.120 --> 06:34.580
Did you feel anything from it?

06:35.120 --> 06:37.620
No, it was the same as always.

06:37.960 --> 06:41.000
You don't know why the resonance was high?

06:41.630 --> 06:46.420
I think I shared my brother's feelings at that time.

06:47.470 --> 06:49.220
Your feelings were one?

06:49.220 --> 06:50.180
Yes.

06:51.010 --> 06:53.800
We had the same feelings of not
wanting to lose the ones we loved.

06:56.520 --> 07:02.020
We didn't know what to do,
but we wanted to do something.

07:02.020 --> 07:06.190
It sounds silly saying that,
but that's what I thought at the time.

07:06.900 --> 07:09.030
And I think my brother had the exact same feeling.

07:11.410 --> 07:13.160
But I wonder if that was really the case.

07:13.700 --> 07:17.370
He felt quieter—or rather, further than he usually is.

07:19.830 --> 07:20.960
Kasane-san?

07:20.960 --> 07:23.170
Oh, sorry. It's nothing.

07:33.390 --> 07:36.600
I promise I'll defeat the Corpse with my brother

07:38.560 --> 07:41.310
so that the Lightless Stone can be yours.

07:41.850 --> 07:45.020
And when you get that,
Sasame and Emiru will come back, right?

07:45.650 --> 07:46.820
I'm sure my brother will too.

07:49.490 --> 07:51.450
That's what I wanted to tell you.

07:59.870 --> 08:02.000
I'm sure there's a way.

08:03.250 --> 08:04.540
So please...

08:05.290 --> 08:08.380
Don't go anywhere, Aoshi.

08:11.920 --> 08:13.470
To our hard work!

08:21.270 --> 08:25.980
With Natsuiri dead, the technical stuff is all on you.

08:25.980 --> 08:27.400
Really, thanks for the hard work.

08:27.980 --> 08:32.400
I don't know what I'll be able to do, but I'll try my best to do what I can.

08:32.990 --> 08:35.740
That's parroting Aoshi-kun, isn't it?

08:35.740 --> 08:37.490
It's what Akashi said.

08:38.330 --> 08:43.000
That he shared Aoshi's feelings on the Argent.

08:43.000 --> 08:44.370
I see.

08:45.080 --> 08:48.340
So even after all that, he's still the same.

08:50.420 --> 08:56.840
And right now you're thinking to yourself, "Why are
you two understanding each other after denying me?

08:56.840 --> 08:58.510
Not really.

08:58.510 --> 09:01.720
I knew he loved his brother way too much.

09:02.310 --> 09:06.100
He's thinking that part of being
a man is to not make you worry.

09:09.610 --> 09:12.820
What the Lightless Realm took
was a heavy burden on everyone.

09:13.280 --> 09:16.570
Nobody knows what they should be doing.

09:18.660 --> 09:23.330
You should do your best to get Aoshi-kun back to normal.

09:24.210 --> 09:25.710
I think that's how it should be.

09:32.210 --> 09:33.090
Kasane?

09:33.090 --> 09:34.720
Susan...

09:34.720 --> 09:35.670
What's wrong?

09:36.510 --> 09:37.180
Aoshi...

09:39.430 --> 09:43.560
Aoshi's LIM is somehow acting strange.

09:43.560 --> 09:44.600
Strange?

09:44.600 --> 09:45.850
How so?

09:45.850 --> 09:50.360
All sorts of little details are different from before.

09:51.150 --> 09:52.940
I'm scared of obtaining new data.

09:56.860 --> 09:57.820
I'm sorry.

09:59.200 --> 10:01.490
I'm sure it's just me.

10:01.490 --> 10:03.120
I must be tired.

10:03.910 --> 10:05.290
Let's drink some more, Susan.

10:10.210 --> 10:16.630
I've told you many times before, but it's wrong to blame yourself for him heading into the Lightless Realm.

10:17.130 --> 10:19.510
That was of Aoshi-kun's own will.

10:20.550 --> 10:22.050
And?

10:22.050 --> 10:27.770
In short, isn't the persona copy on
the resonance module incomplete?

10:27.770 --> 10:29.520
<i>And</i>?

10:29.520 --> 10:36.030
So we should repeat the resonance testing
with Saginuma Aoshi to make it more certain.

10:36.030 --> 10:38.780
If we do that, it'd take forever to get anywhere!

10:40.320 --> 10:42.530
But if something goes wrong...

10:42.530 --> 10:44.950
Aoshi-kun said he wanted to go!

10:44.950 --> 10:46.750
But if something—

10:46.750 --> 10:49.370
If he doesn't, it all stays as one big hypothesis!

10:49.370 --> 10:51.170
We need solid evidence!

10:51.420 --> 10:56.420
He wants to help with your research since he loves you.

10:57.260 --> 11:02.850
I can't just stomp all over the feelings of someone like that.

11:06.850 --> 11:08.520
Want me to piggyback ride you?

11:08.520 --> 11:09.560
I'm fine.

11:12.730 --> 11:15.900
Yeah, I did say that to Natsuiri-san.

11:16.610 --> 11:18.280
You don't regret it?

11:19.280 --> 11:25.370
I'm honestly scared of going there,
but if I can do it, I don't want to run away.

11:26.080 --> 11:29.660
And I've seen you toil away on the new Vess research.

11:30.290 --> 11:33.830
So I'd like to think I can affect that research most.

11:35.380 --> 11:37.630
I'll be sure to return with results.

11:38.590 --> 11:41.180
I want to show Akashi my awesome side too.

11:44.010 --> 11:48.810
It must be tough, but you're all I've got. I'm counting on you.

11:54.940 --> 11:59.690
There has to be some clue within
the data that Natsuiri kept to himself.

12:04.910 --> 12:07.950
I wish I could get some painkillers from the infirmary.

12:08.580 --> 12:09.540
The hospital...

12:11.910 --> 12:14.000
Could it be <i>that</i> hospital?

12:16.170 --> 12:17.210
It shows up!

12:17.630 --> 12:21.590
That place was supposedly abandoned after the Argent first booted up.

12:24.680 --> 12:27.100
There are no possibilities left.

12:27.100 --> 12:29.100
I have to give it everything I've got.

12:32.270 --> 12:33.640
Abandoned hospital?

12:34.350 --> 12:37.440
Before it became the Argent's development facility,

12:37.440 --> 12:40.320
it was a hospital where they admitted
Necrometal patients from the Lightless Realm.

12:40.690 --> 12:44.820
Natsuiri did all his LIM experiments in secret here.

12:44.820 --> 12:50.700
In other words, Natsuiri kept using it as
his lab after it was completely abandoned.

13:19.940 --> 13:22.360
This is mostly shared data.

13:23.740 --> 13:25.030
What's this?

13:25.030 --> 13:26.030
A server?

13:29.280 --> 13:30.410
This must be it.

13:31.370 --> 13:33.790
The data stored here must be our hope.

13:35.460 --> 13:38.170
Aoshi, wait for me.

13:45.130 --> 13:46.180
This is...

13:46.180 --> 13:47.220
It's the Corpse's...

13:56.440 --> 13:59.860
That hospital had such a shady track record?

13:59.860 --> 14:01.270
Seems that way.

14:01.900 --> 14:03.650
Looks like the Argent's fine.

14:05.900 --> 14:09.450
Big Brother, Kasane-san is doing her best.

14:09.950 --> 14:14.660
She is struggling due to the guilt of
turning you, Emiru, and Sasame into LIMs.

14:16.790 --> 14:19.120
If you knew Kasane-san would struggle

14:20.170 --> 14:26.220
but still wanted to protect her,
then would that be your sin, Big Brother?

14:27.670 --> 14:33.600
If the desire to protect a loved one is a sin,
then how can you be forgiven, Big Brother?

14:39.350 --> 14:40.940
Is that Kasane?

14:40.940 --> 14:43.150
Hurry up and answer, Susan!

14:48.030 --> 14:48.780
Kasane?

14:48.780 --> 14:49.990
Did you find something?

14:49.990 --> 14:51.910
Susan, there's an Admonition!

14:55.580 --> 14:57.160
It's taking it in?

14:57.160 --> 14:58.120
Not good.

14:58.120 --> 14:59.710
If it keeps this up, the server will...

15:05.210 --> 15:06.960
Your quarry's over here!

15:10.550 --> 15:11.800
Come on, over here!

15:11.800 --> 15:13.260
Hurry on over!

15:13.550 --> 15:14.560
An Admonition?

15:14.560 --> 15:16.640
At that hospital, right?

15:16.640 --> 15:17.310
Yes.

15:19.890 --> 15:22.100
What is the ETA to the abandoned hospital?

15:22.100 --> 15:23.400
Thirteen minutes.

15:27.940 --> 15:29.780
The Argent's resonance rate...

15:29.780 --> 15:31.240
This feeling...

15:31.240 --> 15:32.820
It happened once before.

15:32.820 --> 15:34.950
Akashi, are you all right?

15:34.950 --> 15:36.370
Move out of the way.

15:36.370 --> 15:37.370
I'm going on ahead!

15:40.870 --> 15:43.000
Don't be reckless!

15:43.000 --> 15:45.380
Argent's resonance rate has passed the theoretical limits!

15:50.260 --> 15:51.180
Amazing...

15:51.680 --> 15:53.890
It's that strong link again.

15:54.220 --> 15:56.430
In any case, I must do what I can now.

15:56.430 --> 15:57.560
Isn't that right?

15:59.140 --> 16:00.310
What is this place?

16:09.650 --> 16:12.700
It's growing bigger and bigger.

16:12.700 --> 16:13.410
Hurry!

16:56.240 --> 16:57.620
What is this?

16:57.620 --> 16:59.160
It's moving on its own.

17:00.580 --> 17:01.410
Kasane.

17:04.250 --> 17:05.830
Are you unhurt?

17:06.210 --> 17:07.710
The Reaper's talking.

17:08.250 --> 17:08.790
No...

17:09.170 --> 17:10.550
Is that you, Aoshi?

17:12.630 --> 17:16.550
Right now, it feels like this entire machine is my own body.

17:18.140 --> 17:22.060
My legs, my hands, and even my eyes.

17:23.640 --> 17:26.480
I can even see your face clearly.

17:26.480 --> 17:27.650
Aoshi...

17:37.740 --> 17:38.660
I can sense it...

17:39.160 --> 17:42.240
What it wants is a living human body.

17:44.750 --> 17:45.790
You can't...

17:49.960 --> 17:51.670
That voice just now wasn't Akashi.

17:51.670 --> 17:53.130
What's going on?

17:53.670 --> 17:56.510
There's feedback between pilot and LIM.

17:56.930 --> 17:58.840
Protective filters are currently operational.

17:58.840 --> 18:00.800
External data will be cut from the LIM.

18:13.690 --> 18:14.570
Aoshi...

18:21.160 --> 18:23.830
I can do it too. I can do it too.

18:24.580 --> 18:25.330
Aoshi!

18:25.330 --> 18:26.000
Stop!

18:26.000 --> 18:27.210
Don't fight anymore!

18:27.580 --> 18:29.750
That resonance is beyond limits!

18:29.750 --> 18:30.960
It's impossible!

18:32.170 --> 18:35.340
I don't know how much strain it puts on you!

18:35.340 --> 18:36.970
It's too dangerous!

18:36.970 --> 18:38.130
So please...

18:38.130 --> 18:40.050
Don't fight anymore!

18:40.050 --> 18:42.430
Please, Aoshi!

18:43.680 --> 18:46.480
Do what I tell you at least once.

18:49.020 --> 18:50.520
Aoshi...

18:52.020 --> 18:54.780
You're really going to die!

19:02.740 --> 19:03.780
What?

19:04.330 --> 19:07.500
The Argent's LIM has completely shut down?

19:07.500 --> 19:08.660
You've gotta be kidding!

19:10.330 --> 19:11.630
Aoshi...

19:12.920 --> 19:13.790
It can't be...

19:14.880 --> 19:17.420
Big Brother, what's wrong?

19:17.420 --> 19:18.840
Answer me, Big Brother!

19:24.470 --> 19:26.560
Come on, Big Brother!

19:26.560 --> 19:27.350
Dammit!

19:27.350 --> 19:28.560
What are you doing?

19:28.560 --> 19:29.560
Move!

19:29.560 --> 19:30.560
Move for me!

19:31.770 --> 19:33.770
LIMs die?

19:33.770 --> 19:34.940
Impossible...

19:35.440 --> 19:36.480
Mahmu!

19:36.480 --> 19:38.650
The Argent can't fight!

19:38.650 --> 19:40.030
You have to defeat the Admonition!

19:40.280 --> 19:41.910
O-Okay!

19:48.870 --> 19:50.410
Mahmu! Mahmu!

19:54.000 --> 19:55.290
Aoshi!

19:55.290 --> 19:57.750
Aoshi, answer me!

20:00.800 --> 20:01.680
Aoshi!

20:06.600 --> 20:09.140
Aoshi, don't go...

20:10.390 --> 20:13.480
I want you to live forever.

20:14.230 --> 20:16.060
I want you to stay at my side forever.

20:19.190 --> 20:23.240
I want to feel your hand again!

20:39.960 --> 20:40.920
Big Brother...

21:02.190 --> 21:04.400
Kasane...

21:08.780 --> 21:09.870
Aoshi!

21:15.170 --> 21:21.590
I wanted to touch you once more too, but it looks like I'm out of time.

21:22.760 --> 21:23.880
I'm sorry.

21:27.510 --> 21:35.270
Kasane, I want you to hurry and
regain that smile you used to have...

21:51.620 --> 21:52.620
Aoshi...

22:24.110 --> 22:25.150
Big Brother...

22:29.110 --> 22:32.410
Thank you, Aoshi...

22:56.390 --> 23:00.440
You lose your mind, you crash; a nervous breakdown

23:00.440 --> 23:05.190
You feel an urge inside, you crush; there's no escape now

23:05.190 --> 23:10.070
You try to change your life, you jump another let down

23:10.070 --> 23:12.660
But then you hear a voice inside

23:12.660 --> 23:15.950
You gotta open up your vision and see the life bestowed on you

23:15.950 --> 23:18.540
Blinded by reality

23:18.540 --> 23:20.710
Broken ideology

23:20.710 --> 23:23.250
Heart in captivity

23:23.250 --> 23:25.590
Hold on, exceeding the borders within

23:25.590 --> 23:28.090
Seize your capability

23:28.090 --> 23:30.470
Endless possibility

23:30.470 --> 23:32.800
Find your individuality

23:32.890 --> 23:35.010
Take pride; let the chase begin

23:35.010 --> 23:37.680
Don't tell me what direction you think I should take

23:37.680 --> 23:39.480
I know now to find the way

23:39.480 --> 23:42.480
Don’t tell me that this sable is for my own sake

23:42.480 --> 23:44.020
Here's what I’ve got to say

23:44.020 --> 23:47.280
Don't tell me to believe the decisions you make

23:47.280 --> 23:49.490
Facing a new day

23:49.490 --> 23:51.490
So open up your blinded eyes

23:51.490 --> 23:54.490
Stop living a lie and start living your life

23:54.490 --> 23:56.830
My way or no way

23:56.830 --> 23:59.290
Today you’re falling away

23:59.290 --> 24:01.620
My way or no way

24:01.620 --> 24:04.920
Today I’m breaking away

24:04.960 --> 24:09.960
Episode 21

24:04.960 --> 24:09.960
You Will, to the Birth Cry of the End
